about: Guides for flashing, unlocking, and recovering selene.

name: Unlocking the bootloader (Example)
status: stable
maintainer: jzadl
date: 2026-02-10
content:
  Unlocking the bootloader wipes your device. Back up everything first.

  1. Enable developer options: settings > about phone > tap build number 7 times.
  2. In developer options, turn on OEM unlocking and USB debugging.
  3. Reboot into bootloader: adb reboot bootloader
  4. Run: fastboot flashing unlock
  5. Confirm on the device screen using the volume keys.
  6. The device will wipe and reboot on its own, this can take a few minutes.

  Once unlocked, fastboot devices should show your device as unlocked.

name: Flashing a custom ROM safely (Example)
status: stable
maintainer: jzadl
date: 2026-02-11
content:
  Requires an unlocked bootloader and a custom recovery already installed.

  1. Download the ROM zip and copy it to the device storage.
  2. Boot into recovery: adb reboot recovery
  3. Take a backup of your current system if you want a way back.
  4. Wipe cache and dalvik, do not wipe internal storage.
  5. Flash the ROM zip, then flash GApps if the build needs them.
  6. Reboot into system. First boot can take several minutes, let it sit.

  If it bootloops, see the bootloop recovery guide.

name: Recovering from a bootloop (Example)
status: stable
maintainer: community
date: 2026-03-05
content:
  Covers a device stuck restarting on its own logo, including EDL mode as a last resort.

  1. Try a factory reset from recovery first, this fixes most bootloops.
  2. If recovery itself won't load, hold power plus volume down for 10 seconds
     to force a reboot, then try entering recovery again.
  3. Still stuck: reflash the stock boot and vendor images from the firmware
     section, this resets the boot chain without touching user data.
  4. Last resort: EDL mode. Hold both volume keys and connect USB, this puts
     the device in a low level flashing mode that can recover a fully bricked
     device using the manufacturer's flash tool.

  EDL mode can restore almost anything short of physical hardware damage.
